Features to Add Later (to make it production-ready)
Retry mechanism: If a vendor API fails, retry a few times before giving up.
Dead Letter Queue (DLQ): Move permanently failed jobs to a separate queue for investigation.
Manual acknowledgments: Acknowledge a message only after the report is successfully generated, uploaded, and emailed.
Prefetch (QoS): Limit how many messages each worker processes concurrently to avoid overloading downstream services.
Correlation IDs: Include a request ID in every message for tracing across logs.
Structured logging: Log each stage (received, processing, uploaded, emailed) with the same request ID.
Monitoring: Track queue length, processing time, success/failure counts, and worker health using Prometheus/Grafana or similar tools.
Idempotency: Prevent duplicate reports if the same message is delivered more than once.
Graceful shutdown: Finish in-progress jobs before stopping workers.
Config management: Keep RabbitMQ, S3, SMTP, and vendor API settings in configuration files or environment variables.

